=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The NOC's premise that the OSPF virtual-link between r4 and r8 has collapsed is incorrect. Live inspection of the Kath5 lab shows the virtual link is fully operational. On r4 (Router ID 14.1.4.1), VLINK0 shows neighbor 18.1.4.1 (r8) in state Full/DROther, established via Area 1 through interface eth1 (45.1.1.1). On r8 (Router ID 18.1.4.1), VLINK0 mirrors the same — neighbor 14.1.4.1 (r4) in Full/DROther, and r8's Area 0 backbone membership is live with one active adjacency (exactly the virtual link). The virtual-link configuration is symmetric and correct: r4 uses `area 1 virtual-link 18.1.4.1` and r8 uses `area 1 virtual-link 14.1.4.1`, matching actual router IDs on both ends.

Area 2 (0.0.0.2) belongs exclusively to r8 — it contains r8's own loopback prefixes (18.1.1.x–18.1.4.x) and the stub interface 80.0.0.0/8 (segment BB). There are no peer routers in Area 2, so zero OSPF adjacencies in that area is the expected steady state, not a sign of failure. All Area 2 prefixes are correctly summarised by r8 as an ABR and appear in r3's backbone routing table. r12 and r13 intentionally run EIGRP (AS 100) rather than OSPF; r11 is the ASBR that redistributes their prefixes into the OSPF domain.

The entire topology — all five OSPF areas (0, 1, 2, 3, 4), all adjacencies, and all inter-area summaries — is healthy. No corrective action is required; the ticket should be closed as a false alarm.
=== END ===